 <mujiburrahimank@lvdocker7.lvsw.maxlinear.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:31:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-104489 Manual Channel Change on Radio 6G Disables
 iw dev and hostapd

Root Cause : 6G interface is down when static channel is set and acs is enabled
The interface failed to come up because the channel change operation failed after an
exclusion list was received from the controller.

During exclusion list processing, hostapd saves the current channel definition (chandef)
onto a stack and restores it when channel exclusion conditions are cleared. While
restoring the chandef, the secondary channel value was incorrectly changed from -1 to 255.

Subsequently, a static channel configuration reused this corrupted secondary channel
value (255) instead of a valid value (-1, 0, or 1), causing the interface to enter an
invalid state and preventing the channel change from succeeding.

Resolution : Updated the secondary channel variable type from uint8 to int in the data structure,
ensuring negative values are preserved correctly during chandef save and restore operations.

System Impact : 6GHz static channel setting

Fixup : WLANRTSYS-50170 [MXL] Smart ACS implementation
---
 src/ap/mxl_acs.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/mxl_acs.h b/src/ap/mxl_acs.h
index 59b8c3cec..34618b709 100644
--- a/src/ap/mxl_acs.h
+++ b/src/ap/mxl_acs.h
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@ int mxl_hostapd_check_and_abort_scan(struct hostapd_iface *iface);
 
 typedef struct {
 	u8 pri;
-	u8 sec;
+	int sec;
 	u8 chwidth;
 	u8 cent_freq;
 	int sel_cand;
